## 12. Hierarchical Clustering

### Python Code (`.py`)
```python
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
from sklearn.datasets import load_iris
from sklearn.cluster import AgglomerativeClustering
from scipy.cluster.hierarchy import dendrogram, linkage

iris = load_iris()
X = iris.data
y_true = iris.target

# Agglomerative Clustering
hc = AgglomerativeClustering(n_clusters=3, linkage='ward')
y_hc = hc.fit_predict(X)

# Cross-tabulation against true labels
ct = pd.crosstab(y_true, y_hc, rownames=['True Species'], colnames=['Hierarchical Clusters'])
ct.index = iris.target_names
print("Cross-tabulation of True Labels vs Hierarchical Clusters:")
print(ct)

# Dendrogram Plot
plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))
dendrogram(linkage(X[:30], method='ward'))
plt.title('Hierarchical Clustering Dendrogram (First 30 Samples)')
plt.xlabel('Sample Index')
plt.ylabel('Euclidean Distance')
plt.show()
```

### Output
```text
Cross-tabulation of True Labels vs Hierarchical Clusters:
Hierarchical Clusters   0   1   2
setosa                  0  50   0
versicolor             49   0   1
virginica              15   0  35

[Generated Hierarchical Clustering Dendrogram plotting Sample Index vs. Euclidean Distance using Ward linkage]
```
